      <Docs>
        <param name="state">one of the DNS_OPTION_* values. Value is one of the following: DnsOptions.DNS_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED; DnsOptions.DNS_OPTION_ENABLED; DnsOptions.DNS_OPTION_DISABLED</param>
        <summary>Sets whether to allow use of stale DNS results when network resolver fails to resolve the hostname.</summary>
        <returns>the builder for chaining. This value cannot be null.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Sets whether to allow use of stale DNS results when network resolver fails to resolve the hostname.</para>
          <para>Depending on the use case, if the DNS resolver quickly sees a fresh failure, it may be desirable to use the failure as it is technically the fresher result, and we had such a fresh result quickly; or, prefer having any result (even if stale) to use over dealing with a DNS failure.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/net/http/DnsOptions.StaleDnsOptions.Builder#setUseStaleOnNameNotResolved(int)" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.net.http.DnsOptions.StaleDnsOptions.Builder.setUseStaleOnNameNotResolved</code>.</a></format></para>
